<refnamediv>
  <refname><function>SilikoNodeGetId</function></refname>
  <refpurpose>Get the function name of a branch node</refpurpose>
</refnamediv>

<refsynopsisdiv>
<programlisting language="C">#include &lt;SilikoCore/Node.h&gt;</programlisting>
<programlisting language="C">const char *SilikoNodeGetId(
    const SilikoNode *object);</programlisting>
</refsynopsisdiv>

<refsection>
<title>Description</title>
<para>The <function>SilikoNodeGetId</function> gets the function name
of <varname>object</varname>.</para>
</refsection>

<refsection>
<title>Return Values</title>

<para><function>SilikoNodeGetId</function> returns a pointer to the
function name held by <varname>object</varname> if
<varname>object</varname> is a branch node, or
<literal>NULL</literal> if not. If a valid pointer is returned, it
remains owned by <varname>object</varname> and must not be deallocated
by the caller.</para>
</refsection>
